cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this artifact, please cite it as below. Cite the third-party components it measures as well (THIRD_PARTY.md)."
title: "Serving a 763B Mixture-of-Experts Model on Workstation GPUs: A Measurement Study of Expert Offload in vLLM"
version: "0.1.0"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Abrego"
    given-names: "Javier"
    affiliation: "Inferencekey"
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - vLLM
  - mixture of experts
  - EXL3
  - quantization
  - host memory offload
  - LLM serving
  - benchmarking
  - reproducibility
repository-code: "https://github.com/inferencekey/vllm-exl3-moe-hostoffload"
abstract: >-
  A measurement study of serving DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash (763B parameters, 3-bit EXL3 experts) with vLLM, the vllm-exl3
  plugin and Diffbot's host-memory expert offload recipe on two 96 GB RTX PRO 6000 GPUs: attribution audit, static
  byte accounting, controlled experiments on fit, speed, long context, quality and coding-agent concurrency, and the
  LaTeX paper, with every number generated from its data file. Code Apache-2.0; text and data CC-BY-4.0.
date-released: "2026-10-12"
# doi is added once Zenodo archives the release (RELEASE_CHECKLIST.md)
